  "dom_id": "step-q82230",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find an expression for the volume $V$ of a cylinder in terms of $r$ given that $\\frac{r}{h}=7,$ where $r$ is the radius of the base and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.",
  "worked_solution": "Our goal is to express $V$ in terms of $r.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $h$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =7 \\\\ r & =7h \\\\ \\frac{r}{7} & =h \\\\ h & =\\frac{r}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $h=\\frac{r}{7}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi {r}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{r}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi {r}^{3}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
